phosh-osk-data (0.58.0) experimental; urgency=medium

  * ci: Use recent image.
  * packaging: Fix typo.
  * data-packager: Support plain packaging format.
    This gets the files verbatim and installs them to `~/.local/share/`.
    Useful on immutable images.
  * doc: Use `POS_LANG`. `LANG` is used by locales so it is set and may lead to
    funny error messages.
  * doc: Fix indent
  * doc: Import punkt_tab as well. This is at least needed on Debian Trixie
  * manpage: Mention `plain` mode
  * Bump the default version to download
  * build: Build with meson.
    Drop make, this gives us a nice dist tarball for free
    Closes: https://gitlab.gnome.org/World/Phosh/phosh-osk-data/-/work_items/4
  * ci: Check meson format.
    We add our shared-scripts for that
  * ci: Add workflow rules.
  * ci: Add check job for plain too.
  * ci: Move sanity check to style-checks.
  * ci: Separate build from packaging step.

 -- Guido Günther <agx@sigxcpu.org>  Sat, 03 Oct 2026 17:13:32 +0200

